From a9347a785aa5d2ed44b863a242f8bb86d7d88949 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 05:21:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Requeue bound mid-turn owner storage refusals
 without charging card failures

Why: admitted exit-1 WorkerPersistenceError storage_unavailable receipts fell
through the owner-unavailable exit-kind gate and spent the card crash budget.
The earlier host-refusal coverage exercised startup/pre-admission only.

Recognize only the newest exact run/claim bound-interpreter result with the
complete managed worker exception envelope and exit 1. Keep local persistence
errors, stale-generation handling, and the neutral-streak breaker unchanged.
Reuse the host notice window; describe an interrupted turn truthfully.

Proof: regression red before (consecutive_failures 1 instead of 0), green after;
48 focused tests pass. Eleven exact-anchor proof guard mutants killed.
Read-only old/new replay across 20 live board/shadow DBs: 1015 exit-1 crash
records, 12 changed records / 6 unique cards, all bound terminal owner-storage
refusals. Includes all four 01:03:37Z incident cards. No live rows modified.
Deployed replay remains NO_PROOF until the merged build is installed.
